sentences.i:
I asked the one who made me sick, for a kiss to heal the pain;
he said, No, no, never! I said to him, Yes, yes.
Then he said: Take it freely from me, lawfully; and he smiled.
I said, By force. He said, No; only in kindness and generosity.
So ask no more of what passed, but beg God’s pardon and sleep;
think what you will of us, for love grows sweet through suspicion;
and after this I care not whether an enemy blab or keep silent.
